    "body": "Depends on: D3 observation run (#3 in this chain). The teacher's ceiling bounds everything downstream; SmolLM2-135M is a weak teacher by design. Evaluate one larger pinned HF revision (e.g. SmolLM2-360M or Qwen-class llama-family with unsharded BF16 safetensors) through the full pipeline (download → observe → compile → cover → score → Gate C) and compare teacher floor bits/token and graph agreement against the 135M run. Acceptance: a recorded decision on the default teacher with both ceiling tables; if adopted, the pinned revision and HEAD teacher CID are updated in one commit.\n\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n- One larger pinned HF teacher (unsharded BF16 safetensors, llama-family) is run through the full pipeline (download → observe → compile → cover → score → Gate C).\n- A default-teacher decision (stay on 135M vs adopt the larger pin) is recorded with both ceiling tables.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Teacher-floor bits/token and graph top-1 agreement reported for both teachers on the same D3 partitions.\n- [ ] Artifact sizes and per-token latency included in the comparison.\n- [ ] If adopted: pinned revision + HEAD teacher CID updated in one commit with the table attached.",
